You can create a table from, or upload rows into a table from, these file types:

* **CSV** (.csv): the first line has the column names.
{{# for (const [name, imp] of Object.entries(scState.importers)) { }}
* **{{ name }}** ({{ imp.extensions.join(", ") }}): read by a plugin.
{{# } }}

When a table is created from a file, the column types are guessed from the
first rows of the file. Some plugins set the types themselves, for example
dates and coordinates.

When uploading into an existing table, columns are matched to fields by
name or label. A preview shows the rows that will be imported before
anything is saved.
